# Example ReRDMFT input file: LiH, 6-31G, GNOF, FULL_OPTIMIZATION TRUE, CHOLESKY TRUE, FCIDUMP
# TRUE -- the CHOLESKY TRUE counterpart of lih_gnof_fcidump.inp, same system, same functional.
# With CHOLESKY TRUE the packed AO two-electron tensor is released once its Cholesky vectors are
# built (see prepareNonRelEri, main.cpp): FCIDUMP's two-electron integrals then come from those
# vectors (Utils/AoCholesky.h's aoCholeskyToMoSpinOrbital) instead of the exact AO tensor
# (Utils/MoIntegralTransform.h's moTwoElectronSymmetric), through the same templated writeFcidump
# (Utils/Fcidump.h) either way. Converged energy matches lih_gnof_fcidump.inp's exactly; the
# individual two-electron integral elements agree to the Cholesky decomposition threshold
# (CHOLESKY_THRESHOLD, default 1e-10) rather than machine precision.
NELEC 4
BASIS lih-6-31g.gbs
NON_RELATIVISTIC TRUE
CHOLESKY TRUE
FUNCTIONAL GNOF
PNOF_SUBSPACES 2
PNOF_COUPLING 2
FULL_OPTIMIZATION TRUE
FCIDUMP TRUE

GEOMETRY
Li  0.000000   0.000000   0.000000
H   0.000000   0.000000   1.594900
END
